\text{The general relaxation rate in terms of the potential is:}
$$ \frac{1}{\tau} = \frac{n_{imp} m}{4\pi \hbar^3 k_F^3} \int_0^{2k_F} k^3 |V(\mathbf{k})|^2 dk $$
\text{Taking the small-}k \text{ limit } V(\mathbf{k}) \approx V(0) \text{ for the screened Coulomb potential, the integral evaluates to } 4k_F^4 |V(0)|^2 \text{, yielding:}
$$ \frac{1}{\tau} = \frac{n_{imp} m k_F}{\pi \hbar^3} |V(0)|^2 $$
\text{Using the Thomas-Fermi screening wavevector } k_s^2 = e^2 N(\epsilon_F)/\epsilon_0 \text{ (SI) or } 4\pi e^2 N(\epsilon_F) \text{ (CGS), we have } V(0) = \frac{Z}{N(\epsilon_F)} = \frac{Z \pi^2 \hbar^2}{m k_F} \text{. Substituting this gives the fully explicit, unit-independent form:}
$$ \frac{1}{\tau} = \frac{n_{imp} Z^2 \pi^3 \hbar}{m k_F} $$

